Ladybird takes a relatively positioned inline’s extent on a line that
holds a block it contains from that block’s margin box, so an abspos
box positioned against the inline starts where the line does. Each
engine places it there too, from the inline’s own pieces: Blink’s
inline_containing_block_utils unites the inline’s items on its first
and last line boxes, Gecko’s AbsoluteContainingBlock walks the
inline’s continuations and skips the block siblings of an IB split,
and WebKit’s PositionedLayoutConstraints reads the inline’s line
boxes through InlineIterator::lineLeftmostInlineBoxFor().
